USAF PFRA (Physical Fitness Readiness Assessment)
Replaced the ACFT here on 2026-08-17. The old ACFT version of this file was deleted.
Composite out of 100. Pass = 75 total AND every component minimum. 90+ = Excellent.
Tested twice a year (scored of record from 1 Jul 2026).

Four components, and what each is worth:

1. Cardiorespiratory - 50 pts
   Two-Mile Run, or 20m HAMR shuttle. -> running the 2-mile.
2. Body composition - 20 pts
   Waist-to-height ratio (waist inches / height inches). Not trained by this plan.
3. Muscular strength - 15 pts
   Push-ups 1 min, or Hand-Release Push-ups 2 min. -> running 1-min push-ups.
4. Core endurance - 15 pts
   Sit-ups 1 min, or Cross-Leg Reverse Crunch, or Forearm Plank.
   -> undecided, sit-ups or plank. Targeting the sit-up number for now.


